#. Tag: title
#: doclinks.docbook:11
#, no-c-format
msgid "Document Links"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: doclinks.docbook:12
#, no-c-format
msgid "document links"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: doclinks.docbook:14
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kword; has the ability to insert Internet addresses, email addresses, "
"locations within the current document (bookmarks) and external file "
"locations with a descriptor. This is most often used to create web pages in "
"&kword;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: doclinks.docbook:17
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Once inserted into the document, the descriptor will be visible in &kword;, "
"but when saved as a web document, the descriptor will become the hyperlink "
"for the location specified with the address."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: doclinks.docbook:20
#, no-c-format
msgid "Insert a new document link"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: doclinks.docbook:21
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To insert a document link select <menuchoice> <guimenu>Insert</guimenu> "
"<guimenuitem>Link...</guimenuitem> </menuchoice> from the menubar. This will "
"bring up a small dialog box."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: doclinks.docbook:33
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Using the icon bar on the left, choose which link type you want to insert."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: doclinks.docbook:34
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the comment field, type the text you want to appear in your web document "
"(for example: The KOffice Web Site)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: doclinks.docbook:35
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the address field, type the Internet address, email address or file "
"location you want the comment to be linked with (for example: http://www."
"koffice.org)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: doclinks.docbook:37
#, no-c-format
msgid "Click <guibutton>OK</guibutton>."
msgstr "Clicatz sus <guibutton>Validar</guibutton>."

#. Tag: para
#: doclinks.docbook:38
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"By default, &kword; displays links underlined (as in most browsers). You can "
"turn this behavior on and off by selecting <menuchoice> <guimenu>Settings</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>Configure &kword;...</guimenuitem></menuchoice> from "
"the menubar and selecting the <guilabel>Misc</guilabel> page. More "
"information can be found <link linkend=\"opt-misc\">here</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: doclinks.docbook:43
#, no-c-format
msgid "Opening a document link"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: doclinks.docbook:44
#, no-c-format
msgid "You can use a document link from within &kword;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: doclinks.docbook:45
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Simply click once on the document link with the &RMB;. A popup menu will "
"appear. Select <guilabel>Open Link</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: doclinks.docbook:46
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A document link to a web site will open a new browser window and take you "
"directly to that web site. A document link to an email address, will open a "
"new message in your email program. A document link to a file will open the "
"appropriate viewer or editor for that file type."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: doclinks.docbook:51
#, no-c-format
msgid "Copy a document link"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: doclinks.docbook:52
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can use a document link in another application, by copying it from a "
"&kword; document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: doclinks.docbook:53
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Simply click once on the document link with the &RMB;. A popup menu will "
"appear. Select <guilabel>Copy Link</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: doclinks.docbook:54
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The link address has now been inserted into the clipboard. You can paste "
"your clipboard entry into any other application."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: doclinks.docbook:56
#, no-c-format
msgid "Changing a document link"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: doclinks.docbook:57
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To change the details of a document link Simply click once on the document "
"link with the &RMB;. A popup menu will appear. Select <guilabel>Change "
"Link...</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: doclinks.docbook:59
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Insert Link</guilabel> dialog box will appear, with the "
"current settings of the link displayed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: doclinks.docbook:67
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Make any appropriate changes and click <guibutton>OK</guibutton> to make "
"your changes."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: doclinks.docbook:69
#, no-c-format
msgid "Deleting a document link"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: doclinks.docbook:70
#, no-c-format
msgid "You can delete a document link like any other text in your document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: doclinks.docbook:71
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Simply place the cursor at the end of the document link, and press "
"&Backspace;. Alternatively, place the cursor at the beginning of the "
"document link and press <keycap>Delete</keycap> on the keyboard. The "
"document link is deleted in its entirety."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: doclinks.docbook:74
#, no-c-format
msgid "Converting a document link to text"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: doclinks.docbook:75
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If a document link is no longer needed as a link, but you want to preserve "
"the text that is the link, click once on the document link with the &RMB;. A "
"popup menu will appear. Select <guilabel>Remove Link...</guilabel>. The "
"linked text will now become plain text, and the link will be deleted."
msgstr ""
